---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic emotional_1>>
<<SetBGSprite "HutInterior">>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Baba… two minutes?

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Smiling">>
ShivPrasad: Two minutes become twenty with you boys—say it.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: We want your yes for the academy trial in Matunga.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: I said no to the coach, and that no still stands.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: Baba… may I speak?

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Speak, but don't sell me dreams on credit.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: I won't sell dreams—I'll pay in work, keep my lane inside my head, study first, and never forget who I am.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Words are light; bus fare is heavy. What will you give up to carry this?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I will get up with the first bell, practice only when you say, keep homework clean, and help warm your towel before anything.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: I'll escort him, Baba, and adjust my hours—prize money after ground repairs can cover bus for a while, and if sums don't add up, we stop straight.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Prize money blinks and disappears, but school marks stay on the wall—what about those?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: We'll guard them with evening study sessions, and if the page is messy, the ground is off-limits—same rule as before.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Recite your six tables—quick.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Six-ones six, six-twos twelve, six-threes eighteen, six-fours twenty-four, six-fives thirty, six-sixes thirty-six, six-sevens forty-two, six-eights forty-eight, six-nines fifty-four, six-tens sixty.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Spell "discipline."

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: D-I-S-C-I-P-L-I-N-E.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Meaning?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Doing the right thing even when no one is watching.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: The city is watching, little one—waiting for you to slip so it can laugh.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: And then clap, Baba—we won't answer with our mouths, we'll answer with habits.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Habits don't hold umbrellas in rain—if the bus is late and shifts are angry?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Then we skip that day with no heroics or lies—safety and school first, because the academy is a door, not our roof.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: And inside your head, what will you carry when boys older than you push and glare?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Five coins, Baba—eyes, feet, hands, timing, temper, and I'll be a good teammate first because we don't let poverty steal our manners.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Your coach talks smooth, you talk steady—steady is better, but my "no" is about plates and nights, not pride.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: Make it a conditional yes, then. Give us a line we must cross before we step onto that turf.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: You want a line—books first, then bus, because if the boy can carry books like a man, he can carry a bat like one.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Tell me the line, Baba.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Exams are coming, and you will score ninety percent—clean, not eighty-nine with stories. If you do, I will say yes to the academy trial and walk you to the banyan myself.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Accepted.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Earning is louder than pleading—from tomorrow, your timetable is a wall, and Ramu, you guard it.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Ramu" "Neutral">>
Ramu: I'll guard it, Baba.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I'll climb it, one mark at a time.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Good—now put that bat face up and show me today's handwriting.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Face up, chin up—I'm ready.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: We shall see—ninety, Raju, not because a coach asked, but because your future did.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Ninety—I'll bring it home.

<<SetCharacterExpression "ShivPrasad" "Serious">>
ShivPrasad: Then go wash your hands—tea is getting cold, and promises are warmer when made clean.

<<HideAllCharacters>>
<<EndEvent>>
<<StopBackgroundMusic>>
